page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Current chapter library and individual review</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="chapters/chapter.en.css"><style>.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(250px,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.card{padding:1.3rem;background:white;border:1px solid #d0e0dd;border-radius:12px}.card h2{font:450 1.55rem Newsreader,serif;margin-top:0}.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto;background:white;border-radius:10px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}th,td{text-align:left;padding:.8rem;border-bottom:1px solid #dbe7e2}th{background:#eaf3ef}td:nth-child(2){min-width:230px}.filters{display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:1rem 0}.filters input,.filters button{font:inherit;padding:.6rem;border:1px solid #b4ccc4;border-radius:7px;background:white}.filters button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#dceee6}a{text-decoration:none!important}</style></head><body><main class="chapter"><p class="top-link"><a href="index.html#library">Weekly plan and full library</a></p><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Current inventory · 17October2026</p><h1>Chapter library and individual review</h1><p><strong>25 of60 existing editions reviewed · 35 reviews remain.</strong></p><p>The technical library now contains62 of119 planned chapters, including the Projection and Least Squares drafts.57 newtechnical chapters remain. Author review and student approval are recorded separately.</p></header><section class="cards"><article class="card"><h2>Bayes' Rule</h2><p>Latest individual revision:65 reviewed answers,63 expanded derivations,80 final decisions and31 exact problem figures. Population and equal-weight assumptions are explicit.</p><a href="chapters/s_bayes.html">Read the revised chapter</a><p><a href="reviews/s_bayes-current-review.html">Read the evidence and source boundaries</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>Least Squares</h2><p>New author-review draft:22 teaching sections,50 worked mathematical/course problems,one authentic doctoral revisit,60 final decisions and20 compact mechanism-specific placements.</p><a href="chapters/l_leastsquares.html">Read the new chapter</a><p><a href="reviews/l_leastsquares-quality.html">Read its coverage and audit</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>IELTS Academic</h2><p>Three actual60-minute teaching lessons cover grammar,reading and listening. Each has six original synthetic clips. Sessions2and3are prepared ahead; alllearner mastery remains unconfirmed.</p><p><a href="ielts/academic-01-sentences.html">Session1:Sentences and evidence</a></p><a href="ielts/academic-02-routines.html">Session2:Routines and timetables</a><p><a href="ielts/academic-03-nouns.html">Session3:Objects and precise information</a></p></article></section><h2>The original60-chapter review inventory</h2><p>The table tracks individual review of the earlier library. New Projection and Least Squares drafts add to the library without inflating this baseline's reviewed count. Next existing review:Gaussian Elimination. Next new technical authoring:Game Search.</p><div class="filters"><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Find a chapter" aria-label="Find a chapter"><button data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All60</button><button data-filter="checked" aria-pressed="false">25 reviewed</button><button data-filter="pending" aria-pressed="false">35 pending</button></div><p id="result-count" aria-live="polite">60 chapters shown</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Chapter</th><th>Worked entries</th><th>Current review state</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+rows+'''</tbody></table></div><section class="card"><h2>What a checked review means</h2><p>Documented written courses from at least four universities,declared mathematical scope,complete solutions,appropriate diagrams or simulations,and recorded mathematical and rendering checks. Finite audits do not establish literal100percent correctness or guarantee every unseen examination result. Exact source provenance and remaining uncertainty are stated in each audit.</p><p>The latest local drafts and cloud backup are tracked separately from Site publication. Offline copies,GitHub backup and Site publication are separate delivery records;the latest publication result is recorded in the delivery log.</p></section></main><script>let filter='all';const input=document.getElementById('search');function update(){let n=0;document.querySelectorAll('tbody tr').forEach(r=>{r.hidden=!((filter==='all'||r.dataset.state===filter)&&r.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(input.value.toLowerCase()));if(!r.hidden)n++;});document.getElementById('result-count').textContent=n+' chapters shown';}input.addEventListener('input',update);document.querySelectorAll('[data-filter]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{filter=b.dataset.filter;document.querySelectorAll('[data-filter]').forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(x===b)));update();});</script></body></html>'''
